KZ2 patch 6050 (fix, ENHANCEMENT side): keys keep their action under every pad layout.

Report (0.1.6): "F aims down sights and the right mouse button is melee", while the docs say the mouse buttons fire and
zoom. Root cause: keybinds.ini binds keys to pad buttons (patch 2037: l1 = F "close combat", r3 = Mouse2/V "zoom,
flashlight", the game's Standard 1 meanings), but the game maps actions to buttons through the player profile, which
the in-game controller scheme (Alternate 2: zoom L1, close combat R3) and the port's Modern layout (KZ2_PAD_LAYOUT,
same two swapped) rewrite. The keys followed the buttons, so under those layouts F zoomed and the right button meleed.
Fix: pad_kb_roles.h (new, pure) and cellPad.c: pad_kb_set_roles(table, valid_ms) takes, from the title port, the button
each key's Standard action is on in the live profile (port/kz2: kz2_kb_roles from the profile map at 0x011B0540+0x240
-> +0x64, refreshed by the on-foot look update 0x00173E80, valid 300 ms); pad_merge_keyboard maps the keys through it;
pad_kb_key_for_input (keycap prompts) shows the key whose action lands on the prompt's button. A key keeps the
button it got when it went down until it comes up (pad_kb_roles_latch): the table can lapse under a held key. Menus, vehicles and
mounted guns, where the look update does not run, keep the plain buttons (menu accept and back are buttons). Pads and
keybinds.ini are unchanged (every edit keeps working; a key bound to "l1" now means "close combat" on foot).
